# Bundled Gemini MCP server: dist/ IS committed (no ignore rule for it below —
# node_modules/ stays ignored via the top-level `node_modules/` rule above). The
# published plugin marketplace ships exactly what's in git — there is no
# install/build lifecycle hook — so if dist/index.js isn't tracked, a fresh install
# gets `Cannot find module .../dist/index.js` / CONNECTION_CLOSED (regressed at
# v0.6.2, confirmed broken through v0.7.0). esbuild.config.mjs bundles
# @modelcontextprotocol/sdk and @google/genai INTO dist/index.js (`external: []`)
# with a `createRequire(import.meta.url)` banner shim, so google-auth-library's
# internal dynamic `require()` calls still resolve under ESM output — dist/index.js
# is therefore fully self-contained and node_modules is NOT needed at runtime (see
# scripts/check-mcp-dist.sh, which proves this by running dist/index.js alone with
# no ancestor node_modules anywhere). Only test-build output stays ignored.
plugins/academic-writer/mcp/gemini-server/dist-test/

# Local API key fallback (per gemini integration spec)
.academic-helper/secrets.json

# --- Shareability: local session/harness state and personal content ---
# This repo is meant to be shareable as a plugin. Anything below is either
# machine-local state or the maintainer's own content, and carries the home path,
# session ids, or personal drafts. Untracked 2026-09-02; files remain on disk.
# Enforced by scripts/check-no-private-refs.sh so it cannot creep back.
.claude/state/
.claude/memory/
.claude/agents/
.claude/context/
.claude/orchestration/
.claude/HANDOFF.md
.instance/
.removal-log/
past-articles/
logs/
pitch-*.md
*-pitch-*.html

# ALE run dirs and task worktrees (local)
.ale/runs/

# --- Internal dev-process state (maintainer-only; not part of the shareable plugin) ---
